00:30:29.140 --> 00:30:59.110
<v Ira Glass>And this is the kind of magic Blaine's been cultivating for years now. He still does card tricks and all kinds of regular closeup magic, but he's also doing a bunch of effects that are like eating glass. There's no trick to it. He just really does this stuff. It's real. He was sealed in a box suspended above the Thames River for 44 days. He lived in a block of ice for over 60 hours. He held his breath for 17 minutes underwater and then explained his techniques for doing it in a Ted Talk. He works on these things for years, trains his body to do this stuff.
<v Ira Glass>这就是布莱恩多年来一直在培养的魔术类型。他仍然做纸牌魔术和各种常规的近景魔术，但他也在做一系列像吃玻璃这样的效果。这没什么把戏。他真的在做这些事情。它是真实的。他曾被封在一个悬挂在泰晤士河上的盒子里44天。他在冰块里住了超过60个小时。他在水下屏住了呼吸17分钟，然后在TED演讲中解释了他的技巧。他多年来一直致力于这些事情，训练他的身体来做这些东西。

00:30:59.110 --> 00:31:28.890
<v Ira Glass>And then this funny thing happens. Because he's a professional magician, which is to say his job is to deceive people, when he's actually doing these incredible physical feats that aren't tricks, people often think they are. Like he's caught a bullet in his mouth on stage-- a real bullet fired from a real gun. He caught it in this metal cup that he held in his mouth, filmed the bullet traveling in slow motion, filmed his friends seeming actually upset with him for even trying this, and still some people think, nah, that's not real.
<v Ira Glass>然后发生了一件有趣的事。因为他是一名职业魔术师，也就是说他的工作就是欺骗他人，所以当他真正做出那些并非戏法的惊人身体壮举时，人们往往以为那也是戏法。比如他在舞台上用嘴接住了一颗子弹——一颗从真枪中射出的真子弹。他用含在嘴里的金属杯接住了子弹，拍下了子弹飞行的慢动作画面，也拍下了他的朋友们因为他尝试这种事而感到真正不安的模样，可即便如此，还是有些人认为：不，那不是真的。

